17592186204325 1069 "q-223208" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204325 1071 "An object vibrates vertically. The distance between the object and its central position, in millimeters, can be modeled by a function of the form $D(t) = A\\sin (Bt)$, where $A$ and $B$ are constants and $t$ is the time (in seconds). Assume that the positive direction is upward.\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0.1$, the object is at its maximum height, $5$ millimeters above its central position. Then, after $0.3$ seconds, the object reaches its minimum height of $5$ millimeters below its central position.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $D(t)$?" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204325 1072 #uuid "ba987bec-c9bf-5b8c-aa9f-cb47b9e82b4b" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204326 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200749 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204326 1069 "q-223212" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204326 1071 "A heart pumps blood in and out of its chambers. The volume of blood in the heart, in milliliters, can be modeled by a function of the form $V(t) = 35\\cos (Bt) + C$, where $B$ and $C$ are constants and $t$ is the time (in seconds).\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0$, the heart contains its maximum volume of blood, $140$ milliliters. Then, after $1.5$ seconds, the heart contains its minimum volume of blood.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $V(t)$?" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204326 1072 #uuid "702e797c-2a31-5bca-b448-9210d66bb91d" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204327 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200755 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204327 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200760 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204327 1069 "q-223636" 13194139533375 17592186045585 true] [17592186204327 1071 "Prove the following theorem:\n\n> Let $a$ and $b$ be integers and $n$ be a positive integer. If $a$ and $n$ are coprime, and $x_{1} ∈ N$ is a solution to the linear congruence